{'symbol': 'VRSK', 'date': '2021-09-03 09:00:00', 'title': 'AER LEADS STUDY TO REVEAL EXTREME WINTER WEATHER IS RELATED TO ARCTIC CHANGE', 'text': 'LEXINGTON, MASS., SEPT. 03, 2021 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- A NEW STUDY SHOWS THAT THE FREQUENCY OF POLAR VORTEX DISRUPTIONS THAT IS MOST FAVORABLE FOR EXTREME WINTER WEATHER IN THE UNITED STATES IS INCREASING, AND THAT ARCTIC CHANGE IS LIKELY CONTRIBUTING TO THE INCREASING TREND. LED BY ATMOSPHERIC AND ENVIRONMENTAL RESEARCH (AER), UNIVERSITY MASSACHUSETTS LOWELL AND THE HEBREW UNIVERSITY OF JERUSALEM, THE STUDY IS PUBLISHED IN THE SEPTEMBER 3 ISSUE OF SCIENCE . AER IS A VERISK (NASDAQ:VRSK) BUSINESS.'}{'symbol': 'VRSK', 'date': '2021-09-03 07:16:00', 'title': "VERISK'S AIR WORLDWIDE ESTIMATES INSURED LOSSES FOR HURRICANE IDA WILL RANGE FROM USD 17 BILLION TO USD 25 BILLION", 'text': "BOSTON, SEPT. 03, 2021 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- EXTREME EVENT MODELING FIRM AIR WORLDWIDE ESTIMATES THAT INDUSTRY INSURED LOSSES TO ONSHORE PROPERTY RESULTING FROM HURRICANE\xa0IDA'S WINDS AND STORM SURGE WILL RANGE FROM USD\xa017\xa0BILLION TO USD\xa025\xa0BILLION.\u202fAIR WORLDWIDE IS A VERISK (NASDAQ:VRSK) BUSINESS."}